# Local worker development only. Copy to `.dev.vars` and fill in.
#
#   cp .dev.vars.example .dev.vars
#
# `.dev.vars` is gitignored. Wrangler loads it automatically for
# `wrangler dev`. It is NOT how production secrets are set — see DEPLOY.md:
# production uses `wrangler secret put`, and the values live in Cloudflare,
# never on disk and never in a file.
#
# Leave a line commented out to exercise the "not configured" path, which is
# a real state the code handles.

# Not needed locally: outside production, Turnstile is verified only when a
# key is present. Uncomment to test the verification path for real.
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=

# Without this the form answers 502 and shows the "didn't send" state —
# which is the correct behaviour, and worth seeing at least once.
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# REPORT_TO_EMAIL=you@example.com
# REPORT_FROM_EMAIL=robot@yourdomain

# Any non-empty string works locally; production wants `openssl rand -hex 32`.
RATE_LIMIT_SALT=local-development-salt-not-for-production

# Only needed to exercise the scheduled check against a real repository.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=
# GITHUB_REPO=kos-me/by.gold

# `production` makes Turnstile mandatory. Leave as-is locally.
ENVIRONMENT=development
